Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:16:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Support PyTorch kernels and count kernel launches

Parse kernel base names that contain "(anonymous namespace)" or lambdas:
cut the argument list at the first '(' outside template arguments.

KL_HOOK_COUNTS=<file> counts launches per kernel base name and writes
"<count>\t<name>" lines, most launched first, to <file> at exit.

Build with -Wl,--as-needed: the hook dlopens HIP and HSA itself, and the
libamdhip64 that hipcc links would be a second runtime next to an app's own
(e.g. the one PyTorch bundles in torch/lib). Document KL_HOOK_HIP_LIB_PATH
and KL_HOOK_HSA_LIB_PATH under their real names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
